=== CRITERION 1 — engine-inflated amount, discounted at month Year*12 with the
=== SAME ordinary-annuity (m+1) convention; no second discounting formula ===
PASS.

(a) Implementation read: /home/darrell/bin/ai/budget2/internal/services/retirement/analysis/present_value.go
    lines 74-89. The leg delegates entirely:

        for year := range oneTimeYears {
            chargeMonth := year * 12
            if chargeMonth >= months { continue }
            pvExpenses += presentValueOfMonthlyStream(func(month int) float64 {
                if month == chargeMonth { return engine.OneTimeExpensesForYear(s, year) }
                return 0
            }, discountRate, months)
        }

(b) No second discounting formula — mechanically confirmed:
    $ awk 'NR>=74 && NR<=89' .../present_value.go | grep -n 'math\.\|Pow\|\^\|/ *(1'
    output: "NO discount arithmetic inside the leg — it delegates to
             presentValueOfMonthlyStream"
    (grep matched nothing; the leg contains zero rate/exponent arithmetic).
    presentValueOfMonthlyStream (lines 198-213) is the single formula:
    monthlyRate := engine.MonthlyCompoundFactorFromDecimal(discountRate/100) - 1
    pv += amt / math.Pow(1+monthlyRate, float64(m+1))   <-- the (m+1) convention.

(c) Engine rule confirmed at source — internal/services/retirement/engine/expense.go:59
    total += e.Amount * compoundedFactorFromPercent(s.InflationRate, float64(currentYear*12))
    and engine/math.go:30-35  math.Pow(1+annualRatePercent/100, months/12.0)
    i.e. exactly the rule the criterion names. The leg calls
    engine.OneTimeExpensesForYear rather than re-deriving it.

(d) Tests run with -v (scratch copy $SP/z1, -count=1):
    $ go test ./internal/services/retirement/analysis/ -count=1 \
        -run 'TestPresentValue_.*OneTime|TestPresentValue_IncludesOneTimeExpense' -v
    --- PASS: TestPresentValue_IncludesOneTimeExpense (0.00s)
    --- PASS: TestPresentValue_OneTimeExpense_ZeroDiscountRate (0.00s)
    --- PASS: TestPresentValue_OneTimeExpense_AtOrBeyondHorizonContributesNothing (0.00s)
        --- PASS: .../#00 (0.00s)
        --- PASS: .../#01 (0.00s)
    ok  budget2/internal/services/retirement/analysis  0.007s

(e) MUTATION PROOF that the (m+1) convention is actually guarded, not merely
    present. In $SP/z1 the leg was replaced with its own inline discount using
    exponent chargeMonth (not chargeMonth+1):
        amt := engine.OneTimeExpensesForYear(s, year)
        mr := engine.MonthlyCompoundFactorFromDecimal(discountRate/100) - 1
        if mr > 0 { amt /= math.Pow(1+mr, float64(chargeMonth)) }
        pvExpenses += amt
    Result:
